    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nTemporarily exclude five auxiliary-loss test functions (30 parameterized cases) from development CI using function-level `flaky_in_dev` markers:\n\n| Function | Cases |\n| --- | ---: |\n| `test_force_balanced_aux_loss` | 5 |\n| `test_seq_aux_loss` | 5 |\n| `test_seq_aux_loss_mbs_invariant_per_token_loss` | 10 |\n| `test_global_aux_loss` | 5 |\n| `test_combined_aux_loss` | 5 |\n\nAll five functions reinitialize model parallel after `TestRouterAuxLoss.setup_method` has initialized it, exposing the shared process-group teardown/reinitialization race tracked in #7745. LTS eligibility, parameter values, assertions, and test bodies are preserved.\n\nThe confirmed recurring failure is in `test_force_balanced_aux_loss`: after #8206 quarantined `[8-1-1]`, [merge-queue job 116102125211](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/actions/runs/38630673719/job/116102125211) reported a 1,800,000 ms store timeout in `[4-2-1]`. Its source includes the earlier quarantine. The four additional functions are precautionary containment of the shared initialization pattern, not claims of independently observed flakes. This expands the previous one-case exclusion to 30 cases, adding 29 development exclusions in total.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nRelated to #7745; extends #8206 while the initialization fix in #8164 is validated. This quarantine does not fix the race. Keep the issue open and restore coverage after repeated distributed validation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Whole-file AST comparisons verified that quarantine markers are the only semantic changes; all parameters and test bodies are preserved.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Repository autoformat check: Black, isort, pylint, and Ruff passed using repository-pinned versions. Optional mypy reported missing pytest and torch imports in the isolated lint environment.\n- GPU tests were not run for this marker-only change.\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
